 "summary": "[cli] separate definition and values"
 "description": "right now Option holds both configuration parameters - that say how to parese,  \nand values - the result of parsing. this isn't very robust if options are used at places other than main(). for  \nexample, if some server application wants a cli interface (e.g., through a tcp  \nconnection), then the best approach for it would be to have a static variable  \nwith the options configuration and give it to the parser each time."
}

